overflow in sub at i64

The most negative end of `k`, where the lag family is not defined.
`out[i] = xs[i - k]`, and `i - k` overflows i64 once `k` drops below
`len(xs) - 1 - i64::MAX`, so `shift`, `shift_fill`, `shift_clamped`, `diff` and
`pct_change` all trap there rather than returning a series.

That is the `len(xs)` most negative values of `k`, NOT `i64::MIN` alone: the
largest index overflows first, so on this two-element fixture both `i64::MIN`
and `i64::MIN + 1` trap, and `i64::MIN + 2` returns `[None, None]`.

Every less negative `k` is defined: a negative `k` is pandas' lead, `k = 0` is
the identity, and any other out-of-range offset is reported as absence or as
the caller's fill rather than as a trap. The failure is loud, which is why the
docs state the limit rather than the module widening the index type.
